# Access control for the public device listener (1883).
#
# Devices connect anonymously with client-id = their token. `%c` expands to the
# client-id, so each device is confined to its own subtree.

# A device may publish its readings/hello and receive its own commands, and
# nothing else. A leaked token therefore exposes exactly one device: it cannot
# be used to read another unit's data or to forge readings in its name.
pattern readwrite device/sck/%c/#

# Shared registration topic. On boot a device announces its unique hardware id
# here (createInfo(): id / hw_ver / mac / firmware versions) so the backend can
# link a token to a physical unit.
#
# Write-only, and spoofable by anyone who can reach the broker — that is
# accepted. Treat inventory as a HINT to cross-check against what was
# provisioned, never as proof of identity.
pattern write device/inventory
